course: dictionary
lesson: 16012
title: Vascular: tubes that carry things
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Vascular describes tubes that carry things through a living body. In animals, these tubes carry blood. «The doctor checked the vascular system to see how well the blood was flowing.» The clue is blood flowing, so vascular must mean something to do with the tubes that carry blood.
explain: Plants have vascular tubes too. «Ferns are vascular plants, but mosses are not.» Inside a plant, the tubes are called xylem and phloem, and they carry water and food. Mosses have no such tubes, so they are non-vascular.
explain: Use the clue words around the new word. «The vascular bundle carried water up the stem to the leaves.» Bundle, stem, water and leaves all point to tubes that carry things. Swap in your meaning: the tubes that carry things carried water up the stem. It still makes sense, so you are right.
fact: Vascular means to do with tubes that carry things through a living thing.
fact: In animals, the vascular system is made of blood vessels: arteries, veins and capillaries.
fact: In plants, vascular tubes are xylem, which carries water, and phloem, which carries food.
fact: Vascular plants include ferns, trees and flowers. Mosses are non-vascular.
fact: «Vascular surgeons» operate on blood vessels in hospitals.
exercise: «The vascular system carries blood around the body.» What does vascular mean here? | To do with bones and muscles | *To do with tubes that carry blood | To do with breathing air | To do with seeds
exercise: Find the non-vascular plant. Which one has no tubes that carry water and food? | Oak tree | Fern | *Moss | Sunflower
exercise: «The vascular bundle carried water up the stem.» Which word tells you what the tubes carried? | vascular | bundle | *water | stem
test: «Arteries, veins and capillaries are all blood vessels, part of the vascular system.» Which of these is a blood vessel? | Stem | *Artery | Seed | Bone
test: «Phloem is a vascular tube in a plant that carries food.» What does phloem carry? | Water | *Food | Sunlight | Air
exam: «A vascular surgeon operates on the blood vessels inside a patient.» What does a vascular surgeon work on? | Teeth | *Blood vessels | Skin | Bones
